#: ../../source/acl_README.md:1
msgid "*ACL Paper Styles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:3
msgid "This directory contains the latest LaTeX templates for *ACL conferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:5
msgid "Instructions for authors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:7
msgid ""
"Paper submissions to *ACL conferences must use the official ACL style "
"templates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:10
msgid "The LaTeX style files are available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:12
msgid ""
"as an [Overleaf template](https://www.overleaf.com/latex/templates"
"/association-for-computational-linguistics-acl-conference/jvxskxpnznfj)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:13
msgid "in this repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:14
msgid ""
"as a [.zip file](https://github.com/acl-org/acl-style-"
"files/archive/refs/heads/master.zip)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:16
msgid ""
"Please see [`acl_latex.tex`](https://github.com/acl-org/acl-style-"
"files/blob/master/acl_latex.tex) for an example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:18
msgid "Please follow the paper formatting guidelines general to *ACL conferences:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:21
msgid ""
"[Paper formatting guidelines](https://acl-"
"org.github.io/ACLPUB/formatting.html)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:23
msgid ""
"Authors may not modify these style files or use templates designed for "
"other conferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:26
msgid "Instructions for publications chairs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:28
msgid ""
"To adapt the style files for your conference, please fork this repository"
" and make necessary changes. Minimally, you'll need to update the name of"
" the conference and rename the files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:32
msgid ""
"If you make improvements to the templates that should be propagated to "
"future conferences, please submit a pull request. Thank you in advance!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:36
msgid ""
"In older versions of the templates, authors were asked to fill in the "
"START submission ID so that it would be stamped at the top of each page "
"of the anonymized version. This is no longer needed, because it is now "
"possible to do this stamping automatically within START. Currently, the "
"way to do this is for the program chair to email support@softconf.com and"
" request it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:43
msgid "Instructions for making changes to style files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:45
msgid "merge pull request in github, or push to github"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:46
msgid "git pull from github to a local repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:47
msgid "then, git push from your local repository to overleaf project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:48
msgid ""
"Overleaf project is "
"https://www.overleaf.com/project/5f64f1fb97c4c50001b60549"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:49
msgid "Overleaf git url is https://git.overleaf.com/5f64f1fb97c4c50001b60549"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/acl_README.md:50
msgid ""
"then, click \"Submit\" and then \"Submit as Template\" in overleaf in "
"order to ask overleaf to update the overleaf template from the overleaf "
"project"
msgstr ""

